The page turns tilt gravity and shake-to-throw off for good (companionPhysics in
animations.ts): A-NAS's spec has neither, and a tilted tablet would keep a frame loop
running. dsh-pet subscribes to the device's orientation and motion sensors anyway and reads
its two switches in every callback, so that its settings page can turn them on without a new
subscription. A-NAS has no such page, so the card no longer subscribes when both switches are
off; on a tablet or phone the sensors' events no longer run its callbacks many times a second,
during a pause included.

